target: mf log
summary: The history of operations, by label (default: list)

!! Reference

```
The history of operations, by label (default: list)

Usage: mf log [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list    Display the history, by label
  head    Print the id of the newest operation (what `undo --after` takes)
  show    Show full details of one label (a label id, or HEAD for the newest operation's)
  undo    Undo the newest change you made that still stands, by reverting it
  redo    Take the newest undo that still stands back, by reverting it
  revert  Undo a label — what was written inside it — or an operation, by writing its inverse
  prune   Permanently remove operations from the history (irreversible)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
```
